# End-to-end EMULATOR test: BIGTREETECH Octopus Pro v1.0 (STM32H723)
# under Renode in tick mode. Boots real firmware, completes identify +
# clocksync, brings up the full config (4 TMC5160s on software SPI,
# software-PWM heaters, fan, endstops, 2 thermistors) and round-trips
# M114/M105. See "Per-printer tests" in test/emulator/README.md for the
# shared conventions.
#
# Ground specific to this board:
#   - SOFTWARE SPI TMC5160s. klipper's src/stm32/spi.c has no hardware
#     SPI bus for MACH_STM32H7, so H7 boards bit-bang it. Both paths
#     funnel through spidev_transfer (src/spicmds.c), which the
#     renode_hooks TMC SPI chain responder hooks, so it serves the
#     software path unchanged. IOIN version=0x30 proves the round trip.
#   - H7 ADC via stm32h7_adc_stub.py, completing the ISR/CR/SQR1/DR
#     handshake of src/stm32/stm32h7_adc.c. Upstream Renode models the
#     H7 ADC with the F0-family Analog model, which neither matches that
#     handshake nor returns controllable values, so stm32h723.repl omits
#     it and the launcher maps this stub at 0x40022000 instead (the
#     0x400 window also covers the ADC12 common CCR at +0x308).
DICTIONARY stm32h723.dict
CONFIG octopus_pro_h723.cfg
EMULATOR octopus_pro_h723.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

M114
M105
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x30"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc spi"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc spi"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
